-<p>Webull arrived in Malaysia positioning itself as the broker for people who take the US market seriously, deep charting tools, options data, and an aggressive 0% commission push. We looked at whether that positioning holds up, using the same lens we'd apply advising a client on any brokerage platform: regulation first, fees second, features third.</p>
-
-<h2 id="what-is-webull">What Is Webull Malaysia?</h2>
-<p>Webull was founded in the US in 2016 and has since grown into a global brokerage with tens of millions of users across 16 regulated markets. In Malaysia, it operates as <strong>Webull Securities (Malaysia) Sdn Bhd</strong>, offering access to Malaysian stocks, US stocks and options, Hong Kong shares, and China A-shares, the latter being a genuinely uncommon offering among Malaysia-regulated brokers, since direct A-share access for foreign investors has historically been restricted.</p>
-
-<h2 id="regulation">Is Webull Securities (Malaysia) Sdn Bhd Safe and Legit?</h2>
-<p>Yes. Webull Securities (Malaysia) Sdn Bhd holds a <strong>Capital Markets Services Licence (CMSL)</strong> issued by the <a href="https://easy.seccom.com.my:8222/search?name=webull&includeInactive=false" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Securities Commission Malaysia</a> under the Capital Markets and Services Act 2007, and is registered as a Trading Participant of Bursa Malaysia. As with any SC-licensed broker, client assets are covered by the <a href="https://cmcfund.com.my/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Capital Market Compensation Fund</a> for broker-related default, up to RM100,000 per investor. This is not insurance against your investments losing value; no legitimate broker or regulator anywhere offers that.</p>
-
-<h2 id="rewards">2026 Welcome Rewards</h2>
-<p>Webull's current new-user offer (campaign until 31 October 2026, per webull.com.my): keep a net deposit of at least RM5,000 for 60 days to receive RM300 in trading vouchers (3 × RM100). This is Webull's standard campaign; signing up through the <strong>BursaNews referral link</strong> is how Webull records the referral.</p>
-<p>We've laid out the exact deposit requirements and the full step-by-step flow in our <a href="../webull-sign-up-code.html">Webull Malaysia sign-up guide</a>.</p>
-
-<h2 id="fees">Webull Malaysia Fees: Bursa and US Stocks</h2>
-<p>For Malaysian stocks, Webull charges 0.05% commission and zero platform fee. For US stocks, Webull's promotion page lists <strong>0 commission for 365 days</strong> for new users (checked 4 October 2026), a generous offer for anyone trading US stocks regularly. After promotional periods end, low commission rates apply, with no platform fee, no account opening fee, and no inactivity fee.</p>
-<div class="hl-box">💡 Webull also pays interest on unused cash sitting in your account, a detail that's easy to miss but adds up if you keep a cash buffer between trades. Check the current rate in-app, since it moves with market conditions.</div>
-
-<h2 id="features">Key Features Worth Knowing</h2>
-<h3>Fractional Shares and 24-Hour Trading</h3>
-<p>Webull lets you buy US stocks and ETFs with as little as USD 1, useful if you want to start small or dollar-cost-average into expensive stocks without committing to a full share. It also supports trading outside standard US market hours, which matters for Malaysian investors given the time-zone gap with US regular trading sessions.</p>
-<h3>Dual Banking and Shariah Filtering</h3>
-<p>Webull supports both conventional and Islamic banking for deposits, and includes a Shariah-compliance indicator to filter stocks, a genuinely useful feature for investors who need to screen for Shariah-compliant holdings and don't want to cross-reference an external list manually.</p>
-<h3>Research Depth</h3>
-<p>Webull's charting and analysis tools (order book depth, analyst ratings, technical indicators) skew toward users who already know what they're looking at. It's a strength for anyone coming from a more advanced trading background, and a bit more of a learning curve for a first-time investor compared to Moomoo's more guided, AI-assisted approach.</p>
-
