+<p data-en="For Malaysian stocks, Webull charges 0.05% commission and zero platform fee. For US stocks, Webull's promotion page lists <strong>0 commission for 365 days</strong> for new users (checked 4 October 2026), a generous offer for anyone trading US stocks regularly. After promotional periods end, low commission rates apply, with no platform fee, no account opening fee, and no inactivity fee." data-zh="马股方面，Webull收取0.05%佣金，平台费为零。美股方面，Webull优惠页面列明新用户享<strong>365天0佣金</strong>（2026年10月4日查证），对经常买卖美股的人来说相当划算。优惠期结束后适用低佣金收费，且无平台费、开户费或账户闲置费。">For Malaysian stocks, Webull charges 0.05% commission and zero platform fee. For US stocks, Webull's promotion page lists <strong>0 commission for 365 days</strong> for new users (checked 4 October 2026), a generous offer for anyone trading US stocks regularly. After promotional periods end, low commission rates apply, with no platform fee, no account opening fee, and no inactivity fee.</p>
+<div class="hl-box" data-en="💡 Webull also pays interest on unused cash sitting in your account, a detail that's easy to miss but adds up if you keep a cash buffer between trades. Check the current rate in-app, since it moves with market conditions." data-zh="💡 Webull也会为账户里闲置的现金支付利息。这个细节很容易被忽略，但如果你习惯保留一些现金备用，积少成多也很可观。利率会随市况变动，请在App内查看最新利率。">💡 Webull also pays interest on unused cash sitting in your account, a detail that's easy to miss but adds up if you keep a cash buffer between trades. Check the current rate in-app, since it moves with market conditions.</div>
+
+<h2 id="features" data-en="Key Features Worth Knowing" data-zh="值得了解的主要功能">Key Features Worth Knowing</h2>
+<h3 data-en="Fractional Shares and 24-Hour Trading" data-zh="碎股与24小时交易">Fractional Shares and 24-Hour Trading</h3>
+<p data-en="Webull lets you buy US stocks and ETFs with as little as USD 1, useful if you want to start small or dollar-cost-average into expensive stocks without committing to a full share. It also supports trading outside standard US market hours, which matters for Malaysian investors given the time-zone gap with US regular trading sessions." data-zh="在Webull，最低USD 1就能买美股和ETF。如果你想从小额开始，或想定期分批买入高价股而不必买一整股，这非常实用。它也支持美股常规交易时段以外的交易，考虑到马来西亚和美国的时差，这一点对本地投资者很重要。">Webull lets you buy US stocks and ETFs with as little as USD 1, useful if you want to start small or dollar-cost-average into expensive stocks without committing to a full share. It also supports trading outside standard US market hours, which matters for Malaysian investors given the time-zone gap with US regular trading sessions.</p>
+<h3 data-en="Dual Banking and Shariah Filtering" data-zh="双银行体系与伊斯兰教义筛选">Dual Banking and Shariah Filtering</h3>
+<p data-en="Webull supports both conventional and Islamic banking for deposits, and includes a Shariah-compliance indicator to filter stocks, a genuinely useful feature for investors who need to screen for Shariah-compliant holdings and don't want to cross-reference an external list manually." data-zh="Webull支持传统银行和伊斯兰银行存款，并内置符合伊斯兰教义（Shariah）的股票标示和筛选功能。对需要筛选Shariah股票、又不想手动对照外部名单的投资者来说，这功能非常实用。">Webull supports both conventional and Islamic banking for deposits, and includes a Shariah-compliance indicator to filter stocks, a genuinely useful feature for investors who need to screen for Shariah-compliant holdings and don't want to cross-reference an external list manually.</p>
+<h3 data-en="Research Depth" data-zh="研究工具深度">Research Depth</h3>
+<p data-en="Webull's charting and analysis tools (order book depth, analyst ratings, technical indicators) skew toward users who already know what they're looking at. It's a strength for anyone coming from a more advanced trading background, and a bit more of a learning curve for a first-time investor compared to Moomoo's more guided, AI-assisted approach." data-zh="Webull的图表和分析工具（买卖盘深度、分析师评级、技术指标）比较偏向本身已有经验的用户。对有一定交易背景的人来说这是优势；但相比Moomoo更有引导性、结合AI辅助的设计，新手需要多花一点时间上手。">Webull's charting and analysis tools (order book depth, analyst ratings, technical indicators) skew toward users who already know what they're looking at. It's a strength for anyone coming from a more advanced trading background, and a bit more of a learning curve for a first-time investor compared to Moomoo's more guided, AI-assisted approach.</p>
+
+<h2 id="rsp" data-en="New: Webull Flexible RSP (Fixed vs Dynamic Amount)" data-zh="新功能：Webull灵活定投RSP（固定金额 vs 动态金额）">New: Webull Flexible RSP (Fixed vs Dynamic Amount)</h2>
+<p data-en="Webull Malaysia has rolled out its Regular Savings Plan, which the app calls <strong>Recurring Investment</strong>. You pick a US stock or ETF, choose how often to buy (weekly, every two weeks, or monthly), and Webull places the order for you on schedule using the USD buying power already in your account. It takes the &ldquo;when should I buy?&rdquo; decision off your plate, which is where most beginners stall." data-zh="Webull马来西亚推出了定期定额投资计划（RSP），App里称为<strong>Recurring Investment</strong>。你只需选好一只美股或ETF，设定买入频率（每周、每两周或每月），Webull就会按时用你账户里的美元购买力自动下单。它帮你解决了&ldquo;什么时候买？&rdquo;这个问题，而这正是很多新手迟迟不敢开始的原因。">Webull Malaysia has rolled out its Regular Savings Plan, which the app calls <strong>Recurring Investment</strong>. You pick a US stock or ETF, choose how often to buy (weekly, every two weeks, or monthly), and Webull places the order for you on schedule using the USD buying power already in your account. It takes the &ldquo;when should I buy?&rdquo; decision off your plate, which is where most beginners stall.</p>
+<p data-en="What makes it flexible is that you get two ways to decide how much goes in each time." data-zh="它灵活的地方在于，每次投入多少钱，有两种方式可以选择。">What makes it flexible is that you get two ways to decide how much goes in each time.</p>
+
+<div style="overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;">
+<table class="comp-mini">
+<tr><th></th><th data-en="Fixed Amount" data-zh="固定金额">Fixed Amount</th><th data-en="Dynamic Amount" data-zh="动态金额">Dynamic Amount</th></tr>
+<tr><td><strong data-en="Minimum" data-zh="最低金额">Minimum</strong></td><td>USD 1</td><td data-en="Shown in the app when you set up the plan" data-zh="设定计划时在App内显示">Shown in the app when you set up the plan</td></tr>
+<tr><td><strong data-en="How much is bought" data-zh="每次买入金额">How much is bought</strong></td><td data-en="The same amount every time" data-zh="每次相同金额">The same amount every time</td><td data-en="Between 50% and 200% of your base amount" data-zh="基础金额的50%至200%">Between 50% and 200% of your base amount</td></tr>
+<tr><td><strong data-en="What decides it" data-zh="由什么决定">What decides it</strong></td><td data-en="You" data-zh="由你决定">You</td><td data-en="Where a benchmark closed versus its moving average" data-zh="基准指标收盘价相对于其移动平均线的位置">Where a benchmark closed versus its moving average</td></tr>
+<tr><td><strong data-en="Budgeting" data-zh="预算安排">Budgeting</strong></td><td data-en="Fully predictable" data-zh="完全可预测">Fully predictable</td><td data-en="Changes from one buy date to the next" data-zh="每次买入日都可能不同">Changes from one buy date to the next</td></tr>
+</table>
 </div>
+
+<h3 data-en="How Dynamic Amount works, in plain terms" data-zh="动态金额怎么运作？用白话解释">How Dynamic Amount works, in plain terms</h3>
+<p data-en="You set a base amount, then choose a benchmark and a moving-average period. The benchmark can be the stock you are buying itself, or a market index such as the S&amp;P 500, Nasdaq or Dow Jones. Before each purchase, Webull checks the benchmark&rsquo;s previous close against that average. Trading below the average means a bigger buy; trading above means a smaller one." data-zh="你先设定一个基础金额，再选择基准指标和移动平均线周期。基准可以是你要买的那只股票本身，也可以是标普500、纳斯达克或道琼斯等大盘指数。每次买入前，Webull会比较基准指标前一个交易日的收盘价和移动平均线：低于均线就多买，高于均线就少买。">You set a base amount, then choose a benchmark and a moving-average period. The benchmark can be the stock you are buying itself, or a market index such as the S&amp;P 500, Nasdaq or Dow Jones. Before each purchase, Webull checks the benchmark&rsquo;s previous close against that average. Trading below the average means a bigger buy; trading above means a smaller one.</p>
+<p data-en="So with a USD 50 base amount, a single purchase could be as low as USD 25 when the market is running hot, or as high as USD 100 after a sharp dip. Over time you naturally put more money in when prices are lower and less when they are stretched, without having to make that call yourself." data-zh="举例来说，基础金额设为USD 50，市场过热时单次可能只买USD 25，大跌之后则可能买到USD 100。长期下来，你自然会在价格较低时投入更多、价格偏高时投入更少，而不需要自己去判断时机。">So with a USD 50 base amount, a single purchase could be as low as USD 25 when the market is running hot, or as high as USD 100 after a sharp dip. Over time you naturally put more money in when prices are lower and less when they are stretched, without having to make that call yourself.</p>
+<p data-en="Webull Malaysia publishes the exact multipliers it uses:" data-zh="Webull马来西亚公布的标准倍数如下：">Webull Malaysia publishes the exact multipliers it uses:</p>
+<div style="overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;">
+<table class="comp-mini">
+<tr><th data-en="Benchmark vs moving average" data-zh="基准与移动平均线的差距">Benchmark vs moving average</th><th data-en="Below average" data-zh="低于均线">Below average</th><th data-en="Above average" data-zh="高于均线">Above average</th></tr>
+<tr><td data-en="0% to 1%" data-zh="0%至1%">0% to 1%</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr>
+<tr><td data-en="1% to 3%" data-zh="1%至3%">1% to 3%</td><td>120%</td><td>90%</td></tr>
+<tr><td data-en="3% to 6%" data-zh="3%至6%">3% to 6%</td><td>140%</td><td>80%</td></tr>
+<tr><td data-en="6% to 10%" data-zh="6%至10%">6% to 10%</td><td>160%</td><td>70%</td></tr>
+<tr><td data-en="10% to 15% (below) / 10% to 20% (above)" data-zh="10%至15%（低于）/ 10%至20%（高于）">10% to 15% (below) / 10% to 20% (above)</td><td>180%</td><td>60%</td></tr>
+<tr><td data-en="More than 15% (below) / more than 20% (above)" data-zh="超过15%（低于）/ 超过20%（高于）">More than 15% (below) / more than 20% (above)</td><td>200%</td><td>50%</td></tr>
+</table>
 </div>
+<p data-en="Notice the asymmetry: the plan cuts back gently when markets run up, but steps in harder when they fall." data-zh="留意这里的不对称：市场上涨时，计划只是温和地减少投入；市场下跌时，加码的力度却更大。">Notice the asymmetry: the plan cuts back gently when markets run up, but steps in harder when they fall.</p>
+
+<div class="hl-box" data-en="💡 <strong>Our take as ex-bankers:</strong> Dynamic Amount is a disciplined rule, not a crystal ball. A stock trading below its average can keep falling, and buying more of it does not make it a safer company. Pick what you buy carefully first; automation only helps with <em>when</em> and <em>how much</em>." data-zh="💡 <strong>前投行人士的看法：</strong>动态金额是一套有纪律的规则，不是水晶球。跌破均线的股票可能继续下跌，买得多并不会让一家公司变得更安全。先认真挑选要买什么，自动化只能帮你决定<em>什么时候买</em>和<em>买多少</em>。">💡 <strong>Our take as ex-bankers:</strong> Dynamic Amount is a disciplined rule, not a crystal ball. A stock trading below its average can keep falling, and buying more of it does not make it a safer company. Pick what you buy carefully first; automation only helps with <em>when</em> and <em>how much</em>.</div>
+
+<h3 data-en="Costs to keep in mind" data-zh="需要留意的成本">Costs to keep in mind</h3>
+<p data-en="Webull Malaysia lists zero commission and no platform fee on US stocks and ETFs, which is what makes small weekly or monthly buys sensible here. On many other brokers, a minimum fee per trade would eat a big slice of a USD 20 purchase. That said, zero commission is not zero cost. You still pay the ringgit to USD conversion spread, any regulatory and exchange fees that apply, and an ETF&rsquo;s own annual expense ratio. Currency movement also affects what your holdings are worth in ringgit." data-zh="Webull马来西亚列明美股和ETF零佣金、零平台费，这正是每周或每月小额买入在这里划算的原因。在很多其他券商，每笔交易的最低收费可能就吃掉一笔USD 20买入的一大部分。不过，零佣金不等于零成本。你仍需承担令吉兑美元的汇兑差价、适用的监管及交易所费用，以及ETF本身的年度管理费。汇率变动也会影响你的持股以令吉计算的价值。">Webull Malaysia lists zero commission and no platform fee on US stocks and ETFs, which is what makes small weekly or monthly buys sensible here. On many other brokers, a minimum fee per trade would eat a big slice of a USD 20 purchase. That said, zero commission is not zero cost. You still pay the ringgit to USD conversion spread, any regulatory and exchange fees that apply, and an ETF&rsquo;s own annual expense ratio. Currency movement also affects what your holdings are worth in ringgit.</p>
+
+<h3 data-en="How to set one up" data-zh="如何设定">How to set one up</h3>
+<ol>
+<li data-en="Fund your Webull account and convert to USD, so there is buying power ready before the first buy date." data-zh="先存款到Webull账户并兑换成美元，确保第一个买入日之前已有足够购买力。">Fund your Webull account and convert to USD, so there is buying power ready before the first buy date.</li>
+<li data-en="In the Webull app, go to <strong>Markets, then Discover, then RSP</strong>, and search for the stock or ETF you want." data-zh="在Webull App里进入<strong>Markets，然后Discover，再点RSP</strong>，搜索你想投资的股票或ETF。">In the Webull app, go to <strong>Markets, then Discover, then RSP</strong>, and search for the stock or ETF you want.</li>
+<li data-en="Set your amount, pick weekly, bi-weekly or monthly, and choose your investment date. Then select Fixed Amount or Dynamic Amount." data-zh="设定金额，选择每周、每两周或每月，以及投资日期。然后选择固定金额或动态金额。">Set your amount, pick weekly, bi-weekly or monthly, and choose your investment date. Then select Fixed Amount or Dynamic Amount.</li>
+<li data-en="For Dynamic, select the benchmark and the moving-average period, then confirm." data-zh="若选动态金额，再选择基准指标和移动平均线周期，然后确认。">For Dynamic, select the benchmark and the moving-average period, then confirm.</li>
+</ol>
+<p data-en="If you go Dynamic, keep a cushion of up to twice your base amount in USD. A purchase that doubles on a dip will not go through if the cash is not there. Webull sends a push notification the day before each scheduled buy, and you can update or cancel the plan any time before it is processed." data-zh="如果选择动态金额，账户里最好预留最多两倍基础金额的美元。下跌时买入金额翻倍，若现金不足，订单就无法执行。Webull会在每次预定买入的前一天发送推送通知，在处理之前你都可以随时修改或取消计划。">If you go Dynamic, keep a cushion of up to twice your base amount in USD. A purchase that doubles on a dip will not go through if the cash is not there. Webull sends a push notification the day before each scheduled buy, and you can update or cancel the plan any time before it is processed.</p>
+
+<h3 data-en="Which one should you choose?" data-zh="该选哪一种？">Which one should you choose?</h3>
+<p data-en="If you are starting out and want a steady monthly habit, go with <strong>Fixed Amount</strong>. It is simple and easy to budget. If you understand moving averages and can handle contributions that swing from month to month, <strong>Dynamic Amount</strong> lets you lean in a little harder during pullbacks. Either way, a broad, low-cost US index ETF is a more forgiving place to start than a single volatile stock." data-zh="如果你刚开始，想养成每月固定投资的习惯，选<strong>固定金额</strong>，简单又容易做预算。如果你了解移动平均线，也能接受每月投入金额起伏，<strong>动态金额</strong>能让你在回调时多加一点码。无论哪种，从覆盖面广、成本低的美股指数ETF开始，都比单买一只波动大的股票更稳妥。">If you are starting out and want a steady monthly habit, go with <strong>Fixed Amount</strong>. It is simple and easy to budget. If you understand moving averages and can handle contributions that swing from month to month, <strong>Dynamic Amount</strong> lets you lean in a little harder during pullbacks. Either way, a broad, low-cost US index ETF is a more forgiving place to start than a single volatile stock.</p>
 
